      <h2>The Critical Divide: Visa-Exempt vs Non-Exempt Nationalities</h2>
      <p>Spain's Digital Nomad Visa is simple for visa-exempt nationalities and complex for non-exempt ones. This single distinction dramatically affects timeline, cost, and ease.</p>

      <h3>Visa-Exempt Nationalities (Fast Track)</h3>
      <p>These nationalities can enter Spain visa-free for 90 days and apply for the Digital Nomad Visa within Spain:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>USA, Canada, UK, Australia, New Zealand, Japan, South Korea, Singapore</strong>: Enter visa-free, apply in Spain (4-8 weeks)</li>
        <li>EU/EEA citizens: Don't need visa at all (just register)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Non-Visa-Exempt Nationalities (Slow Track)</h3>
      <p>These must apply at a Spanish consulate in their home country <strong>before traveling</strong>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>India, Brazil, Philippines, Nigeria, Pakistan, Vietnam, China, Thailand, Indonesia, and 100+ others</li>
        <li>Must apply at Spanish consulate (4-12 weeks depending on consulate)</li>
        <li>Can't enter Spain until visa is approved</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--red">
        <div class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div>
          <p><strong>CRITICAL:</strong> If you're non-visa-exempt, you cannot just go to Spain and apply. You must apply at a Spanish consulate in your home country (or another country where you have a visa). Processing can be 8-12 weeks. Plan ahead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Income Requirements by Currency</h2>
      <p>Spain requires EUR 2,300/month minimum income from sources outside Spain. For non-EU currencies, this converts as follows (April 2026 rates):</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>USD:</strong> ~$2,500/month (USA, Canada, Australia, UK)</li>
        <li><strong>GBP:</strong> ~£1,900/month (UK)</li>
        <li><strong>AUD:</strong> ~$3,600/month (Australia)</li>
        <li><strong>CAD:</strong> ~$3,150/month (Canada)</li>
        <li><strong>ZAR:</strong> ~R41,000/month (South Africa)</li>
        <li><strong>INR:</strong> ~₹189,000/month (India)</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Note:</strong> Rates fluctuate. These are approximate. Consulates use official rates at time of application.</p>

      <h2>Visa-Exempt Nationalities: The Easy Route</h2>

      <h3>Step-by-Step Process</h3>
      <ol style="list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Arrive in Spain with passport (visa-free 90-day entry)</li>
        <li>Within your 90 days, go to local Immigration Office (Oficina de Extranjería)</li>
        <li>Submit Digital Nomad Visa application + documents</li>
        <li>Wait 4-8 weeks for approval</li>
        <li>Receive 1-year Digital Nomad residency permit</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Timeline & Cost</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Processing:</strong> 4-8 weeks (varies by city and office)</li>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> ~€100-200 visa fee (varies by region)</li>
        <li><strong>Total cost:</strong> €200-400 plus accommodation/living expenses during 90-day wait</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Where to Apply in Spain</h3>
      <p>Major cities have Oficina de Extranjería offices:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Madrid:</strong> National Immigration Office (Dirección General de Policía)</li>
        <li><strong>Barcelona:</strong> Immigration Office (Montcada)</li>
        <li><strong>Valencia, Bilbao, Seville, Málaga:</strong> Provincial immigration offices</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Non-Visa-Exempt Nationalities: Consulate Application</h2>

      <h3>Step-by-Step Process</h3>
      <ol style="list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Locate Spanish consulate in your home country</li>
        <li>Gather all documents (passport, proof of income, accommodation, criminal record check)</li>
        <li>Submit application at consulate (in person or by mail)</li>
        <li>Wait 4-12 weeks for approval (depends on consulate)</li>
        <li>Receive visa in passport</li>
        <li>Travel to Spain and register at Immigration Office</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Consulate Processing Times</h3>
      <p><strong>Known slow consulates:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>India:</strong> 8-12 weeks (heavy application volume)</li>
        <li><strong>Brazil:</strong> 6-10 weeks</li>
        <li><strong>Philippines:</strong> 6-8 weeks</li>
        <li><strong>Nigeria, Pakistan:</strong> 4-8 weeks (depends on embassy cooperation)</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--yellow">
        <div class="msv__alert-icon">💡</div>
        <div>
          <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> If non-visa-exempt, apply at the consulate 3-4 months before your planned departure. Don't wait until your trip is set—consulates are slow and can reject applications if documents aren't perfect.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Documents Required (Vary by Nationality)</h2>

      <h3>Core Documents (All Nationalities)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Valid passport (6 months+ validity)</li>
        <li>Proof of income (contract, invoices, bank statements showing €2,300+/month)</li>
        <li>Accommodation proof (rental lease, Airbnb booking, property deed)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Nationality-Specific Additions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>US, Canada, Australia, UK:</strong> Criminal record check or declaration (requirements vary)</li>
        <li><strong>India, Brazil, Philippines:</strong> Medical certificate, background check, employment verification</li>
        <li><strong>Some African countries:</strong> Embassy certification of documents, birth certificate (certified copy)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where to Get a Criminal Record Check (By Nationality)</h2>

      <h3>USA</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>FBI Identity History Summary Check (online request)</li>
        <li>State police clearance (varies by state)</li>
        <li>Cost: $18-50, 3-4 weeks</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Canada</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Royal Canadian Mounted Police (RCMP) Criminal Record Check</li>
        <li>Cost: CAD $50-100, 5-10 days</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>UK</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) Standard Certificate</li>
        <li>Cost: £18, 7-10 days</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Australia</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>National Police Certificate (Australian Federal Police)</li>
        <li>Cost: AUD $25, 5-10 days (online)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Income Proof Documents</h2>
      <p>Spain accepts:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Employment contract (freelance or remote employment)</li>
        <li>Tax returns (past 2 years showing income)</li>
        <li>Bank statements (3-6 months showing regular deposits matching €2,300/month)</li>
        <li>Client invoices (showing ongoing work)</li>
        <li>Company registration (if self-employed)</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>Best practice:</strong> Combine 2-3 documents. Bank statements alone are sometimes questioned. Employment contract + bank statements is strongest proof.</p>

      <h2>Duration & Renewal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Initial visa:</strong> 1 year</li>
        <li><strong>Renewable:</strong> Yes, after 1 year if income still qualifies</li>
        <li><strong>Total stay:</strong> Can remain indefinitely by renewing yearly</li>
      </ul>

