      <div class="msv__faq">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Which nationalities have the easiest time getting Spain's Digital Nomad Visa?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">EU/EEA citizens don't need a visa at all. For non-EU: US, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea have visa-exempt Schengen entry (90 days), making the visa application process faster (you apply once in Spain, not at consulate). Non-visa-exempt nationalities must apply at a Spanish consulate abroad.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What income do I need for the Digital Nomad Visa?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Spain requires EUR 2,300/month minimum income from sources outside Spain. For non-EU currencies, apply the EUR 2,300 threshold converted to your currency: USD ~$2,500, GBP ~£1,900, AUD ~$3,600, ZAR ~R41,000, CAD ~$3,150.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do I need to apply at a consulate or can I apply in Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">If visa-exempt (US, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, etc.), you can enter visa-free and apply in Spain at a local Immigration Office within your 90 days. If not visa-exempt (India, Philippines, Nigeria, etc.), you must apply at a Spanish consulate before travel.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ How long does the Digital Nomad Visa take?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Visa-exempt nationals (apply in Spain): 4-8 weeks from application. Non-visa-exempt nationals (apply at consulate): 4-12 weeks depending on consulate. Some consulates are slow. Plan accordingly.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What documents do I need?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Core documents: passport, proof of income (contract, bank statements, tax return), accommodation proof. Some nationalities may need: criminal record check (varies by country), birth certificate certification, employment verification. Consulate websites specify nationality-specific requirements.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Can my income be in my home currency or must it be EUR?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Your income can be in any currency (USD, GBP, AUD, ZAR, CAD). You just need to prove EUR 2,300/month equivalent. Bank statements show the amount in your currency; consulate converts using current rates to verify you meet threshold.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
